 Santa Barbara
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Juan Nicolas Herrera \, University of California\, S
 anta Barbara\nHosted by: Daniel Martin\n\nJuan Nicolas Herrera earned hi
 s Bachelor’s in Economics jointly from Universidad del Rosario in Colo
 mbia and the Toulouse School of Economics in France. He also holds a Mas
 ter’s in Public Policy and Development from the Paris School of Econom
 ics and a Master of Arts in Economics from the University of California\
 , Santa Barbara (UCSB). Prior to joining UCSB\, he was a Research Fellow
  in the Research Department of the Inter-American Development Bank. Duri
 ng his graduate studies\, he served as an instructor for undergraduate c
 ourses in public economics and statistics and worked as a research assis
 tant for Professor Alisa Tazhitdinova. His research interests include pu
 blic economics\, housing markets\, labor economics\, and applied econome
 trics. His current research focuses on the incidence of taxation in hous
 ing markets.\n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/care-seminar-juan-
 nicolas-herrera-university-california-santa-barbara
